{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivorabc\/usingivorabc"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC"]]},"metadata":{"title":"Using IvorABC","role":"article","modules":[{"name":"IvorABC"}],"roleHeading":"Article"},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorABC exposes four processing types. Each is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" value type with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no-argument initializer and a single primary method:"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Type","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Method","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Result","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"parse(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"(ABCTunebook, [ABCParser.Diagnostic])","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"normalize(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"(ABCTunebook, [ABCNormalizer.Change])","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"validate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"(ABCTunebook, [ABCValidator.Issue])","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCFormatter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"format(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"type":"table","alignments":["left","left","left"],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCTunebook"},{"type":"text","text":" carries two Boolean state flags that enforce the order of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pipeline:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isNormalized"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"validate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" throws unless this is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValidated"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — ","type":"text"},{"code":"format(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" throws unless this is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"So the canonical order is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"parse → normalize → validate → format","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let (parsed, diagnostics) = try ABCParser().parse(data)","let (normalized, changes) = ABCNormalizer().normalize(parsed)","let (validated, issues)   = try ABCValidator().validate(normalized)","","guard issues.isEmpty","else { \/* handle issues *\/ return }","","let text = try ABCFormatter().format(validated)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"normalize(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"validate(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are idempotent — calling them on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tunebook that is already normalized or validated returns it unchanged — so it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"always safe to run the full pipeline."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Parsing","anchor":"Parsing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser"},{"type":"text","text":" decodes UTF-8 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":" into an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCTunebook"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let (tunebook, diagnostics) = try ABCParser().parse(data)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The parser chooses its own parse policy from the version declared in the input:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"strict","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for files that declare ABC 2.1 or later, and "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"loose","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" for everything"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"else (including unversioned files). In loose mode it recovers from common"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deviations rather than failing, and reports each recovery — along with any"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deprecated forms accepted in either mode — as an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser\/Diagnostic"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Diagnostics are always returned, never thrown; each has a human-readable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["for diagnostic in diagnostics {","    print(diagnostic.message)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Diagnostics cover recoverable situations such as a deprecated tempo form"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Q:120"},{"type":"text","text":"), a duplicate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"%%abc-charset"},{"type":"text","text":", an unrecognized character set, a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"malformed version string, or a skipped unrecognizable line."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Unrecoverable problems are thrown as an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser\/Error"},{"type":"text","text":", for example"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".invalidField(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".invalidKeySignature(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".orphanedContinuation"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unmatchedBeginDirective(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".missingTunes"},{"type":"text","text":". Like all IvorABC errors it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EnhancedError"},{"type":"text","text":" and provides a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["do {","    let (tunebook, _) = try ABCParser().parse(data)","} catch let error as ABCParser.Error {","    print(error.message)","}"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Normalizing","anchor":"Normalizing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer"},{"type":"text","text":" upgrades legacy and deprecated constructs to their ABC 2.1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"equivalents, returning a new tunebook whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isNormalized"},{"type":"text","text":" flag is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ABCVersion.current"},{"type":"text","text":", together with a list of the changes it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let (normalized, changes) = ABCNormalizer().normalize(tunebook)","","for change in changes {","    print(change.message)          \/\/ what was changed","    print(change.tuneIndex ?? -1)  \/\/ which tune, or nil for the file header","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Normalization performs conversions such as:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"E:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (elemskip) and legacy ","type":"text"},{"code":"I:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (information) fields → ","type":"text"},{"code":"r:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (remark).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Deprecated C-form tempos (","type":"text"},{"code":"Q:C=rate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") resolved against the active ","type":"text"},{"code":"L:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"M:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"+name+","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" decorations → the standard ","type":"text"},{"code":"!name!","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" form.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Dropping stale directives (","type":"text"},{"code":"%%abc-charset","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"%%abc-version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"%%decoration +","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer\/Change"},{"type":"text","text":" case ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"clearedBeatMultiplier"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"convertedDecoration"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removedDirective"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"replacedField"},{"type":"text","text":") carries the affected"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value, so you can present a precise change log rather than just a count."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Validating","anchor":"Validating"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator"},{"type":"text","text":" checks a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"normalized","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tunebook against the ABC 2.1"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specification:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let (validated, issues) = try ABCValidator().validate(normalized)","","if issues.isEmpty {","    \/\/ `validated.isValidated` is now true.","} else {","    issues.forEach { print($0.message) }","}"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the tunebook has not been normalized, ","type":"text"},{"code":"validate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" throws","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"ABCValidator.Error.notNormalized","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If any issues are found, the returned tunebook is the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"input unchanged"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isValidated","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" flag stays ","type":"text"},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Fix the issues and validate again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Only when the issues array is empty does the returned tunebook have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"isValidated == true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the prerequisite for formatting and resolving.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator\/Issue"},{"type":"text","text":" describes a specific conformance problem — a missing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or misplaced "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"X:"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T:"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"K:"},{"type":"text","text":" field, an inline field used where it is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"allowed, more than one chord symbol or grace-note group on a single note, or a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shorthand decoration with no defining "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"U:"},{"type":"text","text":" field — and exposes both a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tuneIndex"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Formatting","anchor":"Formatting"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCFormatter"},{"type":"text","text":" serializes a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"validated","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tunebook back to ABC 2.1-compliant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"UTF-8 "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let data = try ABCFormatter().format(validated)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the tunebook has not been validated, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"format(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" throws"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ABCFormatter.Error.notValidated"},{"type":"text","text":". Because the model is validated first,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"formatting itself does not fail on content — round-tripping "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parse → normalize → validate → format"},{"type":"text","text":" reproduces a specification-compliant document."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"The AST model","anchor":"The-AST-model"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The syntactic model is a tree of value types:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":null,"code":["ABCTunebook","├─ version:    ABCVersion?","├─ fileHeader: [ABCHeaderEntry]","└─ tunes:      [ABCTune]","   ├─ header: [ABCHeaderEntry]   \/\/ .directive | .field","   └─ body:   [ABCBodyEntry]     \/\/ .directive | .field | .symbols([ABCSymbol])"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCField","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is an enum with one case per ABC information\/tune field","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":".tuneTitle","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".key","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".meter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".tempo","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".voice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", …). Each case’s payload","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a dedicated, fully-typed value (e.g. ","type":"text"},{"code":".key(ABCKeySignature)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCSymbol","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is an enum covering everything that can appear in a line of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"music: ","type":"text"},{"code":".note","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".chord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".rest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".barLine","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".decoration","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".tuplet","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":".slur","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".chordSymbol","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".inlineField","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and so on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Leaf values are wrapped in small validating types — for instance "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCText"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCReferenceNumber"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCVoice\/ID-swift.struct"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCClef\/Name-swift.struct"},{"type":"text","text":" — each of which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exposes an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValid(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" check and a failable initializer that returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for out-of-range input. Others, like "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCLength"},{"type":"text","text":", validate internally in a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"failable initializer without a public "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValid(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" check. All AST types are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCTunebook"},{"type":"text","text":" equality compares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"version"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fileHeader"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tunes"},{"type":"text","text":" only;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isNormalized"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValidated"},{"type":"text","text":" flags are metadata and are excluded."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Building a tunebook programmatically","anchor":"Building-a-tunebook-programmatically"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can construct the AST directly rather than parsing text. Leaf initializers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are failable, returning "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when their validity constraints are not met:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let refNumber = ABCReferenceNumber(uintValue: 1)!","let title     = ABCText(stringValue: \"Cooley's\")!","let key       = ABCKeySignature.standard(.init(tonic: .e,","                                               mode: .dorian)!)","","let header: [ABCHeaderEntry] = [","    .field(.referenceNumber(refNumber)),  \/\/ X:1","    .field(.tuneTitle(title)),            \/\/ T:Cooley's","    .field(.key(key)),                    \/\/ K:Edor","]","","let tune     = ABCTune(header: header,","                       body: [])!","let tunebook = ABCTunebook(fileHeader: [],","                           tunes: [tune])!"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A directly-constructed tunebook has "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isNormalized == false"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isValidated == false"},{"type":"text","text":", so you must run it through the normalizer and validator before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"formatting or resolving."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Error handling","anchor":"Error-handling"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Thrown errors conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EnhancedError"},{"type":"text","text":" (from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/eBardX\/XestiTools"},{"type":"text","text":"): each has a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"category"},{"type":"text","text":" of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"IvorABC\""},{"type":"text","text":" and a human-readable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Type","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Thrown by","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser\/Error","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ABCParser.parse(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator\/Error","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ABCValidator.validate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCFormatter\/Error","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ABCFormatter.format(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"type":"table","alignments":["left","left"],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Non-fatal results are returned rather than thrown, and each also provides a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"message"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Type","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Returned by","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Also","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser\/Diagnostic","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"parse(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"recovery\/deprecation notices","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer\/Change","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"normalize(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"tuneIndex","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator\/Issue","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"validate(_:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"tuneIndex","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"type":"table","alignments":["left","left","left"],"header":"row"},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Concurrency","anchor":"Concurrency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IvorABC is built for Swift 6 strict concurrency. Every public type — the four"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"processing types and the entire AST — is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" value type, so instances"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can be freely shared across tasks and actor boundaries. The processing types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hold no mutable state, so a single "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCParser"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCNormalizer"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCValidator"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/ABCFormatter"},{"type":"text","text":" instance can be reused for any number of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"concurrent operations."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC\/UsingIvorABC","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Take ABC notation from text to a validated syntax tree, and back to text."}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://IvorABC/documentation/IvorABC":{"role":"collection","title":"IvorABC","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorABC\/documentation\/IvorABC","url":"\/documentation\/ivorabc","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ABC Notation parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorABC/documentation/IvorABC/ABCParser/Diagnostic":{"url":"\/documentati